\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}a & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & b & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the value of $\\,a+b+c,\\,$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =3{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}+4{b}_{3}, \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =3{b}_{1}-3{b}_{3}, \\\\ T({b}_{3}) & =-{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}+3{b}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the coordinates of the images relative to the basis $B:$\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=3,$ $b=0,$ $c=3$ and \n\n$$\na+b+c=3+0+3=6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140369/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6641b2cf-00bc-5542-a566-5b8689f2f2a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140369"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38883/selection/f1a7874b48ddfb1854af964a4be3cdfb55d36656830a3aabccc8582a74355b0d" :answer/id #uuid "759eb3e1-90ed-5ef9-ba82-42328c9d553f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38883/selection/1337ffe3f9a34e86dfdc3eda2cfe5c1712612e6ec55a21b68f68fed9ab0fcf49" :answer/id #uuid "ea8b6f9c-22d0-51e1-83ee-d04e0c39afaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38883/selection/8f8d536e9c0ed68bd2796c160ea2f468b8f595f56cb35e4235503c3ebd98f1c7" :answer/id #uuid "b93f0391-9617-5eb0-b662-63764359de60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :a